---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Support — Notix"
  description="Get help with Notix — AI Note Taker. Contact our support team, report a bug, or ask about your subscription."
  current="support"
>
  <main class="page-main">
    <h1>Support</h1>
    <p class="updated">We usually reply within 1–2 business days.</p>

    <div class="contact-card">
      <strong>Email us</strong>
      <p>For any question, bug report, or feedback:<br>
      <a href="mailto:support@notix-ai.app">support@notix-ai.app</a></p>
    </div>

    <h2>Reporting a problem</h2>
    <p>To help us fix things faster, please include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your device model and iOS version</li>
      <li>The app version (Settings → About)</li>
      <li>What you did, what you expected, and what happened instead</li>
      <li>A screenshot or screen recording, if possible</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Subscriptions &amp; billing</h2>
    <p>Notix Pro subscriptions are billed through your Apple ID. You can manage or cancel your subscription anytime in your device settings: <strong>Settings → your name → Subscriptions</strong>.</p>
    <p>Refunds for App Store purchases are handled by Apple — you can request one at <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com" rel="noopener">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>.</p>

    <h2>Account &amp; data</h2>
    <p>You can delete your account and all associated data directly in the app: <strong>Settings → Account Details → Delete account</strong>. Your account and data are permanently deleted after 30 days; logging back in within that period cancels the deletion.</p>
    <p>For data questions, see our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> or email us.</p>

    <h2>Recording lectures and meetings</h2>
    <p>Notix helps you capture material you are entitled to capture. Rules on recording differ between schools, workplaces, and countries, and in some places everyone in the room has to agree before you start — so check the rules that apply to you before you hit record.</p>
  </main>

  
</Base>
